  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/fc06a4e63f38a315dd3944f65f871cca2dbdddee26ec268e857f79e5f4ab8848.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty ,$ the graph tends to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(4\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x)) & =\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2\\pi ) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
